knext bundled fix for vinext 1.1.0 (dist output)
Upstream: https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/pull/3750
What it fixes: On a Nitro build for a Node-like preset (node, bun), a rewrite whose destination
is a file in `public/` was not served. Nitro serves `public/` with its own static handler ahead
of vinext and gives vinext no ASSETS binding, so the Pages Router answered the 404 page for
`beforeFiles`, `afterFiles` and `fallback` rewrites (the Next.js deploy tests
custom-routes-catchall and i18n-ignore-rewrite-source-locale), and the App Router answered an
empty 200 for a `beforeFiles` or middleware rewrite.
Such a file is now fetched back through the running Nitro app (`globalThis.__nitro__.default`),
whose static handler serves it: the Pages wrapper passes a `publicFileFetcher` on the execution
context, and the App Router SSR entry (Nitro's service) resolves the static-file signal through
it. Only `vite build` on a non-workerd Nitro preset emits this; `/_next/image` is unchanged. A
sub-request that reaches vinext again (Nitro has no such file) ends in a 404, never a loop.
Not covered (upstream either): middleware still does not run for a DIRECT request to a literal
public file on Nitro (cloudflare/vinext#3217, a design question), and App Router `afterFiles` /
`fallback` rewrites to a public file need cloudflare/vinext#3429.
Port difference: upstream edits the body of the Pages `serveFilesystemRoute`; here the Pages
hunk wraps that function from outside, because vinext-3741-nitro-pages-image-optimizer.patch
already rewrote its first branch and must keep recognising itself as applied. Same behaviour:
with no ASSETS binding, a non-`/_next/image` filesystem route goes through the Nitro fetcher.
Retire: delete this file (and its manifest entry) when the pinned vinext is >= the first
release that includes cloudflare/vinext#3750.
Applied by `knext vinext-patches` (runs from the app's postinstall and before `knext build`).

